00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.090 align:start position:0%
 
you  as promised this is part 2 of the Q&amp;A  video you guys asked a lot of questions  so let's jump right in  a lot of you want to know a little bit  more about my education I attended  Stanford University in Birmingham  Alabama  that's Samford not Stanford I'm not that  smart where I studied broadcast and  minored in film production I graduated  with a bachelor's degree in journalism  and mass communication in 2015 where do  you live  right now I live in Dallas Texas believe  it or not not all of us sound like  Cowboys I've also lived in New York Ohio  New Jersey and Connecticut are you alone  or do you have a team I do all of the  actual video making myself by which I  mean writing the script recording and  editing the audio and animating the  video itself however I do have a few  very helpful volunteer researchers whose  work is consistently excellent big  shout-out to the thought squad is  mayonnaise and instrument no and neither  is horseradish how do you come up with  topics well it depends most of the time  a question will just pop into my head  and I'll pursue the topic it's helpful  to be genuinely interested in the world  around us if I'm having trouble thinking  of a topic I'll typically look around  for new discoveries in astronomy as I  think space is a very exciting topic  Wendover productions asked how is it  possible that you real-life lore and  royal ocean film society all know each  other personally and all became  successful youtubers I'll start by  saying I'm very flattered for being  recognized by such a quality youtuber  and if any of you haven't seen one  different videos I encourage you to  check out his channel as for the  question Jo from real life lore andrew  from royal ocean film society and i have  been good friends for a number of years  we all get together once a week with  some other friends to watch and discuss  a film i think our success has come  partly from being around to support each  other and partly from surrounding  ourselves with good company there's a  quote I like that says if you're the  smartest person in the room find a  different room what's with the cow you  know it was kind of an accident I first  used the cow in one of my early videos  about the strangest things to fall from  the sky some people commented that they  liked him so I used him again in another  video and the rest is history he's so  much a part of the channel now that he's  even on my business cards speaking of  the cow he doesn't have a name  leave your vote in the comments for what  we should name our favorite cow can we  see your face I get asked this a lot and  I don't really know why  I mean I'm gorgeous of course but that's  not something I would have thought  people would find so important anyway  I'll be going to playlist live and  VidCon this year so I'm sure I'll be in  some photos or video clips for you all  to see and make sure to come find me if  you'll be there too a lot of people have  asked how I make my videos now I'm not  going to say I uploaded a video  specifically outlining how I make my  videos but I uploaded a video  specifically outlining how I make my  videos but I'll go ahead and reiterate  here because I like you guys  once I've written my script I start by  recording my audio using a zoom h5 I sit  in my closet because it's quiet and I  don't have a studio once my audio is  recorded I'll put it in Adobe Premiere  to cut out all the breaths pauses and  mistakes now Premiere isn't specifically  designed to edit audio but I'm very  familiar with it so I use it if you want  to edit your own audio I recommend  something like Adobe Audition  I export my audio as a WAV file and  import it into after-effects from there  I started a long process of animating  which leads to another question how long  does it take to make a video well it  varies depending on the topic but a  rough estimate is about 15 to 20 hours  from concept to final export what made  you want to start second thought believe  it or not I had a tutorial channel way  back in the early days of YouTube stuff  like how to solve a Rubik's Cube and  little editing tricks of course I had no  idea what I was doing but it was fun  fast forward to about a year ago Joe  from real-life lore and I decided we  both wanted to try again  so we made our channels really it was  because we're both interested in  different aspects of the world around us  and we wanted to share our curiosity  with like-minded people who are your  favorite youtubers of course on the top  of my list a real life lore and Royal  Ocean Film Society then there's wind  over productions Kurt's Kazakh CGP Grey  real engineering alternate history hub  okay there are a lot basically if they  make quality educational videos I like  them other than that I'm a big Pokemon  fan so shady Penguin has to be on the  list did you expect your channel to grow  so quickly absolutely not it came as a  huge surprise I had about 8,000  subscribers before I uploaded my NASA  budget video then I woke up to 25,000  subscribers the following morning it  makes me happy to be able to share  interesting topics with so many people  have you ever thought about selling  merchandise or doing a fan meetup  actually yes those are both on the list  of things I'd like to do in the near  future  if you're interested in either of these  things let me know in the comments so I  can gauge community interest what kind  of books do you read I'm a big fan of  historical nonfiction right now I'm  reading the guns of August which is a  fantastic account of the months leading  up to World War one in today's society  it's very easy to get bogged down with  useless information so it's good to work  through a full book when you have the  time do you do YouTube full time and if  so what did you do before YouTube yes I  make my living off youtube now before I  started my channel I worked in the  camera department at Best Buy which is a  big electronics chain if you're not  familiar the recent YouTube advertising  debacle has affected many full-time  youtubers myself included so if you'd  like to help keep second thought afloat  consider supporting the channel on  patreon one especially thoughtful  comment said how do you think this  opportunity has changed your life where  do you see yourself going forward any  plans for expanding the series types or  staff of the channel while I don't want  to get all sentimental here the  opportunity to pursue making educational  videos for a living is a dream come true  I was very unhappy at my old job and  starting a youtube channel was one of  the best decisions I've ever made as for  my career moving forward I'd like to  continue doing YouTube for as long as I  can and hopefully work with lots of  other great creators along the way as of  right now I don't have any plans to  bring on any official staff especially  with the advertising situation that  being said I'm always open to community  contributions such as research subtitles  and original music and I've saved the  most important question for last  does pineapple belong on Pizza this  question has a long island history and  I'm here to settle it once and for all  the answer is thanks again to everyone  who submitted questions hopefully this  video has answered most of them if not  feel free to ask whatever questions you  have left in the comments below and I'll  try my best to answer them you people  make second thought the amazing family  that it is and for that I thank you  thanks for watching and I'll see you at  500,000  you

